PARITY MAPPING (web → native; values verified by the executed swift test below)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  shell:  <FadeIn><div className="flex items-center gap-4"> … </div></FadeIn>
            → TSFadeIn { VStack { freshnessHeader? ; content } } (web FadeIn →
              TSFadeIn; the bare masthead is NOT wrapped in a panel, matching
              the web source which renders no GlassPanel).
  back:   <Link to="/drives"><ArrowLeft/></Link>
            → DriveDetailHeaderBackButton (arrow.left in a rounded, bordered
              control) → onBack() closure. VoiceOver "Back to drives".
  title:  <h1><Route className="text-cyan-400"/> {startAddress} → {endAddress}
            : t('driveDetail.title','Drive Details')>
            → DriveDetailHeaderTitleBlock: route glyph (Color.TS.accent = cyan)
              + Text(resolvedTitle). routeTitle = "start → end" only when BOTH
              addresses are non-empty (web `startAddress && endAddress`), else
              the localized "Drive Details" fallback.
  subtitle:<p>{vehicleName} · <DateTime date in=vehicle/> · <DateTime time
            in=vehicle showTz/> {endTs && → <DateTime endTime in=vehicle/>}</p>
            → projection.subtitle = "vehicleName · date · startTime tz [→ end]".
              date = formatDate (yMMMd, "Apr 4, 2026"); time = formatTime (jjmm,
              locale 12/24h); tz = tzAbbreviation (zzz, "PDT") appended after the
              start time (web showTz); end-time segment only for a finished drive
              (web `drive.endTs && …`).
  replay: <Link to={`/drives/${driveId}/replay`}><Button variant=ghost size=sm
            icon=Play>Replay</Button></Link>
            → DriveDetailHeaderActionButton(play.fill, "Replay") → onReplay(driveID).
  share:  <Button variant=ghost size=sm icon=Share2 onClick=onShare>Share</Button>
            → DriveDetailHeaderActionButton(square.and.arrow.up, "Share") → onShare().
  nav:    web `<Link>`s + the `onShare` prop → the native parity is three
            injected closures (onBack / onReplay(driveID) / onShare) so the
            feature view performs NO routing or networking itself (the page wires
            them to NavigationStack + a share sheet). Actions wrap on compact
            iPhone widths via ViewThatFits.
  i18n:   driveDetail.{title,replay,share} (web-source parity) + native chrome
            (back/live/stale/offline/updating/loading/unavailable/errorTitle/retry),
            table "DriveDetailHeader". 12 keys, full bidirectional coverage.

STATES (every one renders — verified by the ImageRenderer tests [6]):
  loading → DriveDetailHeaderSkeleton (real back + skeleton title/subtitle + two
            skeleton action chips; Reduce-Motion safe via TSSkeleton).
  content → masthead row (back + title/subtitle + Replay/Share). Two flavours:
            finished drive (subtitle has "→ endTime") and in-progress (no end).
  fallback→ loaded drive with no start/end address pair → localized "Drive
            Details" title (web `!(startAddress && endAddress)` branch).
  empty   → DriveDetailHeaderEmpty (no drive resolved): back + "Drive Details"
            fallback title + a friendly "Drive details unavailable" caption —
            never a blank box.
  error   → DriveDetailHeaderErrorView (web QueryError): back + danger glyph +
            "Couldn't load drive details" + message + Retry → model.refresh().
  stale   → freshness chip (Stale) + ONE guarded auto-refresh; cached masthead stays.
  offline → freshness chip (Offline); cached masthead stays, no refetch.
a11y: title/subtitle combined into one header element with a spoken summary
  (DriveDetailHeaderAccessibility.summary), per-control VoiceOver labels (back/
  replay/share/retry), decorative glyphs accessibilityHidden, Reduce-Motion fill
  gate (TSFadeIn), Dynamic Type via tokens/system fonts.
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"DriveDetailHeader") emitted exactly once
  on appear (asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnce).
binding: P1/S8 DriveDetailHeaderSource seam (production impl over the shared
  DrivingStore + SettingsStore state holders for the vehicle tz/locale); the view
  performs NO networking. Previews/tests use InMemoryDriveDetailHeaderSource.

